{"title":"Noma Security","url":"https://noma.security/blog/","favicon":"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/cropped-rounded-favicon-32x32.png","elements":[{"title":"DockerDash: Two Attack Paths, One AI Supply Chain Crisis","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/DockerDash-Blog-1-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>DockerDash: Two Attack Paths, One AI Supply Chain Crisis</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Screenshot-2025-01-26-at-12.02.08.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Sasi Levi</div>\n                                    <div>Feb 03, 2026</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            Executive Summary Noma Labs discloses the discovery of DockerDash. DockerDash is a critical security flaw in Docker’s Ask Gordon AI (beta)&nbsp; assistant that exploits the entire execution chain from AI interpretation to tool execution. In DockerDash, a single malicious metadata label in a Docker image can be used to compromise your Docker environment through a […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/dockerdash-two-attack-paths-one-ai-supply-chain-crisis/","retrieved":1770076800000},{"title":"53% of our Enterprise Customers Gave ClawdBot Privileged Access over the Weekend (And No One Asked Permission)","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Clawdbot_Social-1-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>53% of our Enterprise Customers Gave ClawdBot Privileged Access over the Weekend (And No One Asked Permission)</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/cropped.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Gal Moyal</div>\n                                    <div>Jan 28, 2026</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            Delve into the Clawdbot agentic AI risks that every enterprise should know. Is the productivity boost worth the potential dangers?                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/customers-gave-clawdbot-privileged-access-and-noone-asked-permission/","retrieved":1769558400000},{"title":"If We Can’t “Solve” Prompt Injection, Is AI Red Teaming Worth It?","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Red-Teaming-Blog-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>If We Can’t “Solve” Prompt Injection, Is AI Red Teaming Worth It?</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Diana.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Diana Kelley</div>\n                                    <div>Jan 26, 2026</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            Uncover the complexities of AI Red Teaming and Prompt Injection. Learn how these concepts shape AI security strategies today.                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/is-ai-red-teaming-worth-it/","retrieved":1769385600000},{"title":"Securing Cursor’s Agent Runtime: How Noma Leverages Cursor Hooks for Real-Time AI Guardrails","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Blog-1024x597.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>Securing Cursor’s Agent Runtime: How Noma Leverages Cursor Hooks for Real-Time AI Guardrails</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Maor-Volokh.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Maor Volokh</div>\n                                    <div>Dec 23, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            As 2025 closes, the era of passive AI assistance is over. With the rise of agentic IDEs like Cursor, AI has evolved from writing snippets to executing shell commands, managing files, and orchestrating complex Model Context Protocol (MCP) ecosystems. This shift gives agents the agency to act, but it also gives them the power to […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/securing-the-agentic-frontier-noma-unveils-the-first-real-time-agent-runtime-security-for-cursor/","retrieved":1766448000000},{"title":"Noma: The Standard for Autonomous Agent Security and the OWASP Agentic Top 10","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/OWASP-Top10-Blog-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>Noma: The Standard for Autonomous Agent Security and the OWASP Agentic Top 10</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/cropped.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Gal Moyal</div>\n                                    <div>Dec 22, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            Moving Your Security Focus from Content to Action The simple “Chatbot” is obsolete. We are now in the age of the Autonomous Agent, with systems that plan, use tools, access sensitive data, and make decisions on their own. As businesses rapidly deploy these agents, the security threat has fundamentally changed. A security breach is no […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/owasp-top-10-agentic-risks-with-noma/","retrieved":1766361600000},{"title":"GeminiJack: The Google Gemini Zero-Click Vulnerability Leaked Gmail, Calendar and Docs Data","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/GeminiJack-Blog-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>GeminiJack: The Google Gemini Zero-Click Vulnerability Leaked Gmail, Calendar and Docs Data</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Screenshot-2025-01-26-at-12.02.08.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Sasi Levi</div>\n                                    <div>Dec 08, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            Noma Labs recently discovered a vulnerability, now known as GeminiJack, inside Google Gemini Enterprise and previously in Vertex AI Search. The vulnerability allowed attackers to access and exfiltrate corporate data using a method as simple as a shared Google Doc, a calendar invitation, or an email.                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/geminijack-google-gemini-zero-click-vulnerability/","retrieved":1765152000000},{"title":"The Definitive Guide to Secure Agentic Identity","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Secure-Agentic-Identity-101-Blog-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>The Definitive Guide to Secure Agentic Identity</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/cropped.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Gal Moyal</div>\n                                    <div>Nov 14, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            &nbsp; View the high-resolution PDF here: Secure Agentic Identity 101                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/the-definitive-guide-to-secure-agentic-identity/","retrieved":1763078400000},{"title":"Atlas Shrugged: Trust Boundaries in the ChatGPT Agentic Browser","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Atlas-Shrugged-Blog-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>Atlas Shrugged: Trust Boundaries in the ChatGPT Agentic Browser</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Diana.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Diana Kelley</div>\n                                    <div>Nov 06, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            Back in the early days of the Domain Name System, engineers joked that DNS stood for “Does Not Secure.” DNS turns the internet from a maze of numbers into a map of names people can actually navigate, but early on, it was also ridiculously easy to abuse. Spoofing attacks and cache poisoning always loomed until […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/atlas-shrugged-trust-boundaries-chatgpt-agentic-browser/","retrieved":1762387200000},{"title":"The Top-Five MCP Security Blindspots Putting Your Organization at Risk","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/MCP-Misconfigurations-Blog-1-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>The Top-Five MCP Security Blindspots Putting Your Organization at Risk</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Gal-Pnini-e1762367829409.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Gal Pnini</div>\n                                    <div>Nov 05, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is rapidly transforming enterprise AI capabilities, enabling agents to interact seamlessly with databases, APIs, and business systems. But this rapid adoption comes with a dangerous blind spot: organizations are unknowingly expanding their attack surface in ways that traditional security tools can’t detect. Unlike traditional software vulnerabilities that affect individual applications, […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/top-five-mcp-security-blindspots-putting-your-organization-at-risk/","retrieved":1762300800000},{"title":"A CISO’s Guide to Agentic Browser Security","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Agentic-Browsers-Blog-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>A CISO’s Guide to Agentic Browser Security</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Diana.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Diana Kelley</div>\n                                    <div>Oct 27, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            The recent release of the ChatGPT Atlas agentic browser from OpenAI marked a big moment in AI and browsing, but Atlas isn’t alone. A wave of browsers built with AI at their core are emerging, from Comet by Perplexity, to Fellou and Dia Browser, agentic browsers are centered on the same idea: your browser isn’t just a […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/a-cisos-guide-to-agentic-browser-security/","retrieved":1761523200000},{"title":"The Noma Agentic Risk Map Delivers Complete AI Agent Visibility and Control","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Cover-blog-Nomas-Agentic-Risk-Map-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>The Noma Agentic Risk Map Delivers Complete AI Agent Visibility and Control</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Maor-Volokh.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Maor Volokh</div>\n                                    <div>Oct 22, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            From Superpower to Shadow Risk AI agents give your business many superpowers. Developers use Cursor to write code at machine speed. Knowledge workers delegate complex tasks to ChatGPT Agents. Business teams build custom automation through low-code platforms like Microsoft Copilot Studio and Salesforce Agentforce. Engineering teams deploy sophisticated agent systems in production across cloud infrastructure […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/agentic-risk-map-ai-agent-visibility-control/","retrieved":1761091200000},{"title":"How Does Prompt Engineering Impact AI Security?","contents":"<img class=\"aspect-[1200/644] object-cover w-full rounded-[10px]\" src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/TAGQ-Series1-Blog-1024x536.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                    <div class=\"mt-[17px]\">\n                        <h4>How Does Prompt Engineering Impact AI Security?</h4>\n                        <div class=\"flex flex-row items-center gap-[18px] mb-[17px]\">\n                                                            <div class=\"relative \n                             \n                             \">\n                                                                            <img src=\"https://noma.security/wp-content/uploads/Diana.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"aspect-square object-cover shadow-author rounded-full border border-noma-bright-blue w-[51px] h-[51px]\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                                                                                                                                            </div>\n                                                        <div class=\"text-sm tracking-[0.07px]\">\n                                <div class=\"text-[14px] tracking-[0.07px] leading-[1.4]\">\n                                    <div class=\"font-bold\">Diana Kelley</div>\n                                    <div>Oct 17, 2025</div>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n\n                        </div>\n                        <p class=\"mb-0 line-clamp-3\">\n                            As any speaker will tell you, one of the most nerve-wracking and rewarding parts of presenting is the open Q&amp;A at the end. Rewarding, because most speakers are there for one reason: to share knowledge with others. When you deliver a talk, you do your best to provide information that the audience will find useful, […]                        </p>\n                    </div>","link":"https://noma.security/blog/how-does-prompt-engineering-impact-ai-security/","retrieved":1760659200000}]}